{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398911-manifest-avatar-defitions-and-limits","id":1398911,"title":"Manifest Avatar, defitions and limits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-25T18:12:45-07:00","id":1398911,"title":"Manifest Avatar, defitions and limits","content":"Hello there, I was giving attention to the Manifest Avatar Merit from the Book of Secrets, but there's a lot of doubts this Merits gaves.<br /> The Merit read as:<br /> <br /> &quot;Manifest Avatar (3 pt. Merit)<br /> For most mages, the Avatar remains a mysterious figure,<br /> goading them from the sidelines and appearing primarily<br /> within a Seeking or during other moments of intense stress.<br /> For you, however, the Avatar is a vibrant presence in your<br /> life, as real to you as anyone else. Essentially a character in<br /> its own right, this manifested Avatar interacts with you on<br /> an almost daily basis. In certain situations, it might interact<br /> with other people, as manifestly real as any other person in<br /> your world.<br /> The Manifest Avatar Merit embodies the Avatar as a full<br /> character under the Storyteller\u2019s control. On its own, this<br /> Merit reflects that Avatar as a person who only the associated<br /> mage can see, hear, and interact with on a physical level; in<br /> conjunction with the Background: Allies, however, the Avatar<br /> becomes a character that everyone can see, hear, and feel. In<br /> both cases, the Avatar may come and go as it pleases, bound<br /> only by the physical laws with which it chooses to be bound.<br /> The physical Avatar\u2019s shell can be injured or killed, but that<br /> in itself does not kill the Avatar \u2013 merely its body. For obvious<br /> reasons, that solid Avatar should have a guise that won\u2019t be<br /> too vulgar or bizarre for the Consensus to endure \u2013 a cloaked,<br /> whispering figure, perhaps, but not a screeching, tentacled<br /> monstrosity. The manifested Avatar\u2019s Traits depend upon the<br /> value of the Allies Background, as well as the physical form of<br /> that incarnation. An equine or lupine Avatar, for instance, will<br /> have different Traits than an Avatar that manifests as a crow,<br /> shadow, mirror, or child.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fine, at 3 points he's something that only appears and interacts with the character, fine,but my questions comes when you buy it as &quot;Allies Background&quot;.<br /> <br /> The background reads as:<br /> <br /> &quot;Allies<br /> In times of need, you\u2019ve got folks who\u2019ve got your back.<br /> These allies might be badass friends, helpful animals, people<br /> 304 Mage: The Ascension 20th Anniversary Edition<br /> with connections they can work in your favor, errand-runners,<br /> or maybe even minor spirits who\u2019ll lend you the occasional favor<br /> if and when they feel like doing so. Generally, this Background<br /> refers to unAwakened humans or fairly intelligent animals (like<br /> a wolf pack or a troupe of apes). They\u2019re probably aware of the<br /> weirder side of your life, but they don\u2019t know the details of<br /> mage society or your true powers unless you choose to endanger<br /> them by sharing those secrets. Whatever their nature, or their<br /> relationship to you, these allies are characters in their own<br /> right, with needs, fears, motivations, and agendas that might<br /> coincide with your mage\u2019s goals but also may occasionally<br /> clash with them.<br /> Each dot in this Background gives you one ally with some<br /> moderately useful abilities, or two allies who essentially run<br /> errands and do busywork. At two dots and above, you can<br /> increase the ability of your moderate allies or buy a larger number<br /> of lesser and moderate allies. If you get two dots, for example,<br /> you could select two moderate allies, get four sidekicks, or<br /> make a single major ally who\u2019s more capable than those lesser<br /> ones. Magick-using Allies count as major ones. If your allies get<br /> killed or wind up quitting your company some other way, this<br /> Background loses the dots that represented those characters<br /> until you recruit new allies to replace the departed ones.<br /> In certain cases, this Background may go higher than five<br /> dots \u2013 see Background Traits Over Five, <span style=\"color:#4A1A71\">(p. 301)</span>. For an array<br /> of characters, see Appendix I.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ok, as you put more points on this Background you both can get a minor kind of stronger allies or a major kind of lesser ones, fine got it, but how I can translate this to the Manifest Avatar Traits, how I'm supposed to measure if is reasonable to Avatar having some kinds and numbers of traits or not?<br /> Also as a Ally he's not ALWAYS manifest and if his body is destroyed he can reform again like materialization right? That's what differs from Avatar Companion? He can for example appear just for you if he wants to like the 3 dot merit even if brought as Ally too? And the last question about that, can the Avatar be built with a Spirit sheet and the Materialize Charm? Is this reasonable?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T01:56:51-07:00","id":1398975,"title":"","content":"Manifest Avatar mostly just gets you an avatar that has a real, physical presence. It doesn't promise any abilities or skills or special powers. The voice that is whispering in your ear is instead a presence in the room, that's it. It doesn't throw lightning or make you breakfast in bed, It just shows up to guide you to ascension from time to time, and then vanishes, like any other avatar.<br /> <br /> If you are hoping for more, that's where Allies comes in. How much they are willing to help depends on how many dots you invest in allies. The way the allies background is written, it's not about stats or anything like that, it's about how useful he is to you. <br /> <br /> Suppose you are in a basement, tied up and without your instruments of magick. You need help. You call out to your avatar, and it appears.<br /> <br /> Scenario 1:<br /> <br /> Roger the Mage: &quot;Hey, I need your help. I'm tied up to a chair and there's a bomb on the table about to blow. You got to untie me!&quot;<br /> <br /> Manifest Avatar, 0 dots in Allies: &quot;Roger, I'm your avatar. I am here to show you the way to Ascension, that's all. I can't interfere. All I can do is say: Look inside you. The answers are always there.&quot; (vanishes from existence)<br /> <br /> Roger the Mage: &quot;Thanks for nothing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Scenario 2: <br /> <br /> Manifest Avatar, 1 dot in Allies: &quot;Roger, you really need to work on not getting yourself into these messes.&quot; Avatar moves around behind the mage and unties his hands. &quot;That's the most I can do... and I really wasn't even supposed to do that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Roger the Mage: &quot;Thanks, avatar, I'll take it from here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Scenario 3:<br /> <br /> Manifest Avatar, 5 dots in allies: &quot;Oh my goodness, Roger! That's a bomb! Let me-&quot; (avatar closes his eyes, and suddenly the timer on the bomb stops) &quot;Now let's get you untied and figure out how to foil Dr. Knevil's dastardly plan!&quot;<br /> <br /> Roger the Mage: You're the best, Avatar!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T06:35:04-07:00","id":1399048,"title":"","content":"Note, someithng omitted from Manifest Avatar in the OP:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Avatar manifesting only for the mage can affect the<br /> material world only when no other characters or devices can<br /> see that entity, </div> </div> </div>So yes..the Avatar *could* untie the mage, technically. Teeechnically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T14:32:28-07:00","id":1399139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398911-manifest-avatar-defitions-and-limits?p=1398975#post1398975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manifest Avatar mostly just gets you an avatar that has a real, physical presence. It doesn't promise any abilities or skills or special powers. The voice that is whispering in your ear is instead a presence in the room, that's it. It doesn't throw lightning or make you breakfast in bed, It just shows up to guide you to ascension from time to time, and then vanishes, like any other avatar.<br /> <br /> If you are hoping for more, that's where Allies comes in. How much they are willing to help depends on how many dots you invest in allies. The way the allies background is written, it's not about stats or anything like that, it's about how useful he is to you.<br /> <br /> Suppose you are in a basement, tied up and without your instruments of magick. You need help. You call out to your avatar, and it appears.<br /> <br /> Scenario 1:<br /> <br /> Roger the Mage: &quot;Hey, I need your help. I'm tied up to a chair and there's a bomb on the table about to blow. You got to untie me!&quot;<br /> <br /> Manifest Avatar, 0 dots in Allies: &quot;Roger, I'm your avatar. I am here to show you the way to Ascension, that's all. I can't interfere. All I can do is say: Look inside you. The answers are always there.&quot; (vanishes from existence)<br /> <br /> Roger the Mage: &quot;Thanks for nothing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Scenario 2:<br /> <br /> Manifest Avatar, 1 dot in Allies: &quot;Roger, you really need to work on not getting yourself into these messes.&quot; Avatar moves around behind the mage and unties his hands. &quot;That's the most I can do... and I really wasn't even supposed to do that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Roger the Mage: &quot;Thanks, avatar, I'll take it from here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Scenario 3:<br /> <br /> Manifest Avatar, 5 dots in allies: &quot;Oh my goodness, Roger! That's a bomb! Let me-&quot; (avatar closes his eyes, and suddenly the timer on the bomb stops) &quot;Now let's get you untied and figure out how to foil Dr. Knevil's dastardly plan!&quot;<br /> <br /> Roger the Mage: You're the best, Avatar!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I got the idea, but I'm talking specifically about this line:<br /> &quot;The manifested Avatar\u2019s Traits depend upon the<br /> value of the Allies Background, as well as the physical form of<br /> that incarnation.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398911-manifest-avatar-defitions-and-limits?p=1399048#post1399048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note, someithng omitted from Manifest Avatar in the OP:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So yes..the Avatar *could* untie the mage, technically. Teeechnically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually I've copied the whole Merit from M20: Book of Secrets, it works exactly like this passage you've put here as long you don't buy as a Ally. And that last part I have no idea how to deal, what kind of Traits it's talking about? The Merit says:<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The physical Avatar\u2019s shell can be injured or killed, but that<br /> in itself does not kill the Avatar&quot;<br /> <br /> With this I can assume the Avatar physical body have Vitality Points and Physical Attributes.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","user":"GothicxXx","date":". 06-26-2020, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T20:23:45-07:00","id":1399197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GothicxXx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398911-manifest-avatar-defitions-and-limits?p=1399139#post1399139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I got the idea, but I'm talking specifically about this line:<br /> &quot;The manifested Avatar\u2019s Traits depend upon the<br /> value of the Allies Background, as well as the physical form of<br /> that incarnation.&quot;<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like the Background, there are no real guidelines. ST has to give Traits to your Avatar just like he would with an Ally. An Ally can have any kind of Traits: A sleeper ally ain't going to have Spheres, but a mage ally would.<br /> <br /> Now, we can *speculate* what kind of Traits should your tipical Avatar have. It would have been nice to have a guide on that, but there's none as far as I know. And Avatars are kinda misterious about what they are and what they can do. All that we know from the Merit it's that the Avatar will have Traits to match the form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T21:26:15-07:00","id":1399201,"title":"","content":"&quot;And the last question about that, can the Avatar be built with a Spirit sheet and the Materialize Charm? Is this reasonable?&quot;<br /> I think it says it somewhere but: Avatars can more or less do whatever, especially with points in allies, so limiting it to charms may be a bit annoying or too much. Just go with what works and what the avatar appears as.<br /> Mage might not even know the appearance of the Avatar = His actual Avatar. A 1-2-3 point Avatar companion, the points being points in allies, might be a random fucking bear that shows up to help you sometimes. Obviously it may just show up when appropriate, outside in the woods, as opposed to whenever, a technocratic stronghold under NY.<br /> <br /> Or maybe your Mage knows its your avatar and the avatar lets you know this and it just shows up Dr Who style to help you whenever it feels like.<br /> It's a broad as fuck merit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T22:45:57-07:00","id":1399212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GothicxXx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398911-manifest-avatar-defitions-and-limits?p=1399139#post1399139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I got the idea, but I'm talking specifically about this line:<br /> &quot;The manifested Avatar\u2019s Traits depend upon the<br /> value of the Allies Background, as well as the physical form of<br /> that incarnation.&quot;<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>See, there is no real limit to what the Avatar is capable of. Mage is even super vague about what the avatar IS, much less whether it can be statted out like a familiar. Imagine for a moment that in the three examples, all 3 avatars are of equal power. It's just a matter of how much the avatar is willing to bring to bear. If you needed a big, scary animal, Allies 1 gets you a small dog, allies 3 gets you something like a wolf, and allies 5 gets you a grizzly bear. That isn't to say the avatar with allies 1 couldn't turn into a grizzly bear... it just won't. Why? Who knows. There are rules. RULES.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T08:48:30-07:00","id":1400748,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much Allies dots you need, to turn you avatar into something like JoJo stand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25259-lastcourier","name":"LastCourier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T17:33:30-07:00","id":1401026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LastCourier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1398911-manifest-avatar-defitions-and-limits?p=1400748#post1400748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how much Allies dots you need, to turn you avatar into something like JoJo stand</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I think 1-2 points of allies represents mundane ---&gt; Sorcerer levels of power. 3 is a mage, I think. 4-5 is some pretty tough stuff.<br /> Maybe 4-5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}